WEBVTT

1
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:09,800
Will any of you
ever actually understand

2
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,040
that my species was never designed
for running.

3
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,720
Come on, Abe, running keeps you fit
and extends your life expectancy.

4
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:18,360
On this last point,
I can only agree with you.

5
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:21,840
My life expectancy will considerably
shorten the second I'll stop running.

6
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:25,840
If my calculations are correct, the
palace of King Zamban is the next left.

7
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,720
Well, I calculate
that you can't calculate.

8
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,640
Nice, let me know when they're gone!

9
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:43,280
I won't last long.

10
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,520
-Stay put Abe!
-Oh, I'm not going anywhere!

11
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,840
Meg, on my signal, step on the gas!

12
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,800
-Wait, what?!
-Are you sure about this?

13
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,680
-Now!
-Alrighty, brace yourselves.

14
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:02,920
Oh boy...

15
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,240
-Well done Meg! Now, hang on to me!
-Why??

16
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:25,000
Am I dead now? Is this heaven?

17
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,760
Ewww... Not heaven.

18
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,640
Woow, the palace of Zamban!

19
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:33,600
The King who raised culinary art
to the status of the art of living.

20
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:37,120
If you ask me, those people have been
more successful at the art of dying.

21
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,320
He had one of his magi design a utensil

22
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,680
that would allow him to swallow
any type of food,

23
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,760
whether poisonous or spoiled, without
suffering the slightest inconvenience:

24
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,280
The Holy Spork.

25
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:48,880
We'll need to climb.

26
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,360
Go ahead, I'll wait for you here.

27
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,120
Oh, don't bother.

28
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,560
Hey, is that my whip?!

29
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:01,640
Crolloq!

30
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,080
Oh, glad to see you still remember me,
Megan...

31
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,840
After leaving me for dead.

32
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:11,320
What? No. I only left you...
But you were definitely alive.

33
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,600
True, but while searching for
the Fountain of Middle Age all alone,

34
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:19,760
I might add, I fell into a pit
and was trapped there for five years,

35
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,200
forced to subsist on tiny insects
and tinier grubs.

36
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:28,600
The only thing that kept me alive was
dreaming about this very moment...

37
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:31,120
What about the tiny insects
and tinier grubs?

38
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,720
Oh sorry, it's your own backstory.

39
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,880
-Flash them all!
-I haven't recharged yet.

40
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:39,880
Wow! I can't believe you're right here
in front of me. I read all about you.

41
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,440
Oh, by the way, I'm Chickenhare.

42
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,400
Ohhh, I know who you are, Chickenhare.

43
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,600
I too read all about you
and Meg's exploits... Blablabla.

44
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:48,760
I'm right here.

45
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,160
Well, it's time for Crolloq
to come back into the spotlight.

46
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:54,200
I've been in the shallows long enough.

47
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,040
No hard feelings Meg!

48
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,960
You'll eventually get used to it
you know,

49
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:05,040
me outdoing you
on future treasure hunts and all...

50
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,040
Crolloq is back!

51
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,800
-Well done boss!
-You're the best!

52
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,000
Miggie, Rolf, let's go!

53
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,440
-Okay boss!!
-Okay boss!!

54
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:24,520
Don't worry Meg, we can't win them all.

55
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:27,280
It's not that, it's...
More complicated...

56
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:29,400
Well at least for once
the ground isn't shaking.

57
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,360
No traps, deadly things
or cliches of the kind.

58
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,240
Which is rather good news.

59
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:37,560
I can't believe that you were friends
with the great Crolloq!

60
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,080
She was on my top three adventurers
when I was a kid.

61
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:43,560
Believe me, being around her every day
wasn't so nice...

62
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,200
Abe? What are you holding?? Is it...

63
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,360
Guys, are you okay?

64
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,840
Yeah, we're fine! What is this stuff?

65
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,800
Tiny letters?!

66
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:03,560
Oh yes, I remember! My mother used to
cook it for me, and made it with...

67
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,160
Burning hot tomato sauce!

68
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:14,320
Abe! What's under the dome?
Anything useful?

69
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:18,320
Yuck, it's a stuffed tomato.
I would say... 3000 years old.

70
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:21,400
"Only a full stomach
will stop the flow of abundance."

71
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,920
Wowowowo, I'm not gonna eat that!

72
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:27,640
Come on, Abe! If it really is the Holy
Spork you won't feel the difference!

73
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:29,880
You can do it, come on!

74
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,720
That's it, you got this!

75
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,040
Close your eyes and do it!

76
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,920
Do it!!

77
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,080
Do it now!

78
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:44,960
I've had worse.

79
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,600
-Aaaabe!
-Aaaabe!

80
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,360
Aaahhh, it's not working!!

81
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,160
What? But my stomach is full!!

82
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,640
A weighing scale?
Ooooh, I get it!

83
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:04,120
Guys! It was just a matter of weight!

84
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,440
Oh right, hold on!

85
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,440
Hang on guys!

86
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,240
You're the one that needs to hang on!!!

87
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,280
I clearly think this is the Universe
telling us that

88
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:51,440
we should stop adventuring and open
a restaurant together instead...

89
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,960
-Are you kidding me?
-We're going to do this forever!

90
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,840
-They're back!
-They're back, they're back!

91
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:29,000
Chickenhare! Chickenhare!
Chickenhare! Chickenhare!

92
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,000
Oooh, he looked at me!

93
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:34,040
What are you talking about?!
We made eye contact!

94
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,680
And you would want to trade this
for a restaurant?

95
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:41,560
Maybe the restaurant can wait...
A little.

96
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,360
-Hey dad!
-Son, you're back!

97
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,360
-Come give your old man a hug!
-Come on dad...!

98
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,200
How was it?
Did you find it?

99
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:04,720
-Did you find the Holy Spork?
-You tell me!!

100
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:08,720
Ooohoho, absolutely stunning!!

101
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,120
Dad, everything okay?

102
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,440
Oh, it's a fake! I knew it! I've got
three words for you guys...

103
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,000
rest... au... rant.

104
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,840
We need to talk. Tonight.

105
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:38,160
Son,
how much do you know

106
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:41,280
about the Groundhog
with the Backward-Facing-Face?

107
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:44,920
They say it gives someone the ability
to change one thing from the past.

108
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,520
And that's one of the most powerful
artifacts in the world.

109
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,720
That's right!

110
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:53,680
Eons ago, Queen Ingrid the Indecisive
ruled much of the known world.

111
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:59,680
She was paralyzed by fears that
she could make wrong decisions.

112
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:03,440
And she remembered the Groundhog's
ability to see the future.

113
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,440
You mean like the ability to tell
if spring will come early, eh?

114
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:09,760
Yes! She decided to find a way
to alter that power

115
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,560
so that they can see
and change the past.

116
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,200
All the groundhogs were captured
for her to conduct her experiments.

117
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:21,640
She spent years on it but eventually,
she figured it out.

118
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:26,480
And the Groundhog with
the Backward- Facing-Face was born...

119
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:31,880
Able to change a specific thing from
our past and thus, change the present.

120
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,680
What did Queen Ingrid change?

121
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:37,280
That was all the irony... Knowing that

122
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:41,200
the Groundhog would only be able to
change one thing from the past,

123
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:44,760
she became even more obsessed about
the past itself.

124
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:48,680
She constantly fretted about
what to change. And...

125
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,840
She slowly went mad. And never used it.

126
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,040
And... That's how the Groundhog
was lost to the world.

127
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:59,920
My great-great-grandfather created
a file in our royal archives.

128
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:03,080
I've never read anything about
the Groundhog's legend.

129
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:06,080
That's because...
Well, I stole the file.

130
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,680
-What?! You stole it, Dad?
-What!! That one is terrible!!

131
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,880
I was worried that my brother Lapin

132
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:13,080
would use it to make it like
I was never born...

133
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:15,240
So that he could become king.

134
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,720
Over the years, I studied the file,

135
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:21,600
trying to find any clue that would
reveal the Groundhog's location.

136
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:25,800
There was a piece of parchment that
had nothing but three holes in it.

137
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:29,560
I used every known process
to reveal anything at all.

138
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,640
-What did you want to change?
-Nothing.

139
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,960
I wanted to destroy the Groundhog.

140
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:37,200
Because changing the past
is a power that nobody should possess.

141
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,240
It could change the world
as we know it.

142
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,400
Well, a world without chocolate liquor
candies would suit me perfectly.

143
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:45,720
Queen Ingrid was very close cousins
with King Zamban.

144
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:49,200
I remembered that when I saw the symbol
at the bottom of the Spork...

145
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:53,160
What if their great treasures
were linked?

146
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:57,080
You mean that the combined magic of
those two artifacts could reveal...

147
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,160
Come on! There are three holes
in this parchment.

148
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,800
Just put the spork in! What's the point
of keeping this suspense going?

149
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,800
Just admit that you're totally excited
about it!

150
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,240
-Never!
-Young people...!

151
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,800
Ooh, the Isle of Idle Hands?!

152
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,280
-Sounds actually kind of relaxing...
-Look!!

153
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,880
Stand watch when the sky's last alight

154
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:29,000
All will be revealed in plain sight

155
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:31,200
Impressive how poetry stands
the test of time.

156
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:34,320
Anyway if the Hamster of Darkness
taught me anything,

157
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:36,840
it's that an X always marks the spot.

158
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,400
And I don't see any...

159
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:39,640
Abe's right.

160
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:43,520
The only thing I know about this island
is that Carl lives here, in Hilly-City.

161
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:46,320
Wait, Carl... the Cartographer?

162
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:48,000
Oh, how convenient!

163
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:51,280
Indeed! Then hopefully
he'll be able to help us with this map.

164
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:52,440
Help us?

165
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,560
I think it's time
I came out of retirement

166
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,640
and joined you guys on an adventure.

167
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,520
You know,
make sure you're not getting too cocky.

168
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:03,280
We'd love to have you.
If you think you can keep up.

169
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,360
Don't you worry about me, son.

170
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:09,240
I forgot more about adventuring
than you guys know!

171
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:12,040
I have to host the diplomats
from Zanubi later this week.

172
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:14,760
But as soon as they're gone,
we'll leave.

173
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:32,840
Ok guys! Are we all set?

174
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,560
Sure thing, Chickenhare. We increased
the difficulty level as you asked.

175
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,680
We made it as tough as possible!

176
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:41,360
You might wanna be extra careful
with the rotating cactus!

177
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,600
Oh yep, this one's pretty vicious!

178
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:44,880
Sure will!

179
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,560
And what's the next adventure
on your bucket list by the way?

180
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:52,240
Sorry guys, but if I tell you,
I'll have to kill you!

181
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,040
He's joking, right?

182
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,880
Let's go!!

183
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,160
Chickenhare, I need to talk to you.

184
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,800
Gina, right? You're an archivist.

185
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:09,880
I'm sorry
but I have to train right now.

186
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:13,000
It's urgent.
I don't know where to start...

187
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:16,600
As my dad always tells me,
"don't think, just blurt"

188
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,120
-I'm your sister Chickenhare!
-What??!

189
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,240
Maybe we should stop the training?

190
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,320
Ouch!!

191
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,960
Oh, I'll take that as a yes.

192
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,440
I'm not King Peter's daughter.

193
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,800
I'm the daughter of your real father...

194
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,960
What do you mean?

195
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,880
Your birth father.

196
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:40,720
How can you be my sister?
You're not a...

197
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:44,400
A chickenhare?
It's true, you are quite unique.

198
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,640
Those feathers...

199
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:50,360
I have a sister!

200
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:52,840
Oh... Oh my gosh,
I have so many questions!!

201
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,040
But first,
let me tell you why I'm here.

202
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:59,840
I'm from...
We're from a hidden island far away.

203
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:04,360
For centuries, our people have been fed
by the Tree of Life.

204
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:07,120
But as time went by, the tree got sick.

205
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:12,080
Since then, it gives less and less
fruits, meaning our people are doomed.

206
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:17,240
The day you came to life,
our father knew you were special.

207
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:21,800
He was also convinced that only a great
adventurer could save the dying tree.

208
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:25,720
So when he heard about this great
and kindhearted adventurer...

209
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,080
My dad!

210
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:30,640
He decided to put you on his path
when you were just a baby.

211
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,640
To be raised as one.

212
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,200
Only you, Chickenhare, can save us.

213
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:50,800
Listen, we all have a part to play.

214
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,840
I was trained in the way of the
Out There -

215
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,320
that's what we call
everything outside of our Island.

216
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:57,320
So that when I came here
three years ago,

217
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,680
I could pass as a native
and get a job as an archivist--

218
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,680
You've been here three years?!
And you didn't say anything!

219
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:05,440
I couldn't distract you
until my plan was ready.

220
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,720
Your plan? What plan?

221
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:10,760
To find the Groundhog
With The Backward-Facing-Face

222
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,680
so we can save our tree.

223
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:15,000
Wait, were you there last night?

224
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,000
For three years,
I tore apart the archives

225
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:21,000
looking for the Groundhog's file, but
I couldn't find a single thing on it.

226
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:22,480
You need to get that map so we can find

227
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:24,200
the Groundhog
With The Backward-Facing-Face.

228
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,680
I can't steal from my Dad!

229
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:28,520
What about our father. Our people?!

230
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:30,560
Let's talk to my dad, explain it...

231
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:35,320
No! You heard him, King Peter thinks
the Groundhog has to be destroyed.

232
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,400
-But if it's destroyed...
-Hey, Chickenhare?

233
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,800
Oh, hey, Dad! Daddio...

234
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,400
My Dad!

235
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:44,880
This is Gina, one of the archivists
at the Royal Adventure Society.

236
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:47,400
That is my only connection to her.

237
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,840
We just met. For the first time...
Ever.

238
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,880
It's a pleasure meeting you,
King Peter.

239
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:55,560
I just came by to introduce myself
to Chickenhare,

240
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,760
tell him what a big fan of his I am.

241
00:15:57,920 --> 00:16:01,280
Yeah!
That's exactly what she was doing!

242
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:04,640
Well, then... Nice to meet you, Gina!

243
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,560
You too!

244
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,760
See you later, dad!

245
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,240
I can't do this!!

246
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:14,360
You have to, Chickenhare.
We all rely on you for our lives.

247
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,440
You're our only hope.

248
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,520
-What's wrong, son?
-Oh, um, nothing.

249
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:31,160
Does it have something to do with today

250
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,040
when you were talking
to that archivist?

251
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,480
No, of course not.

252
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:37,480
You know you can tell me everything,
right?

253
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:41,520
I know dad. Well, it's just...
I've been thinking...

254
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:45,160
What I tell you about thinking?
Just blurt it out, son!

255
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:49,120
About the Groundhog
with the Backward- Facing-Face!

256
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:53,080
Is there a problem with me
coming with you? Because if there is...

257
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:56,840
No, it's not that. It's just, um...
I was thinking that maybe...

258
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,120
We shouldn't destroy it, you know.

259
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:02,640
-Can't it be good to change the past?
-No! I already told you!

260
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,440
-This magic is dangerous!
-How would you know?

261
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,960
Because I know so. What is even
the point of changing the past?

262
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,320
We could save people!

263
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,800
You have no idea
what you're talking about, young boy.

264
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:14,440
Sir, apologies.

265
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:16,440
The Zanubi contingent
is on its way out.

266
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:20,040
Very well, I'm coming right away.

267
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,120
Get this idea out of your head, son.

268
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:27,640
So you're the Chosen One?

269
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,800
And I thought

270
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,320
the search for the Hamster of Darkness
was filled with tropes.

271
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:34,680
But this "chosen one" story
is beyond my wildest expectations.

272
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,080
Abe!

273
00:17:36,800 --> 00:17:40,960
Sorry! No offense, Chickenhare,
but this soufflé is the Chosen One.

274
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:47,160
If that happened to somebody else,
I'd have the perfect retort.

275
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:48,920
So what is the plan?

276
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:53,680
I don't want to lie to my dad. But he
would never let us use the groundhog.

277
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:55,640
My people will be doomed.

278
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:59,520
Well, whatever you decide,
we'll be with you all the way.

279
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,600
Right Abe?

280
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:01,680
Sure! I guess...

281
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:04,040
But if we have to go,
then it's tonight.

282
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:08,000
Ok, fair enough...
I'll make sandwiches.

283
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:23,560
Oh ahahaha, you're it!

284
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:24,720
You're it!

285
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,000
You're it!

286
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:27,480
You're it!

287
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,320
-You're it!
-You're it!

288
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,320
You're it, you're it, you're it!

289
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,600
WOULD YOU STOP IT?!

290
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:35,000
Sorry, boss!

291
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,440
Time out!

292
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,280
What did you learn?

293
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:41,800
That Featherbeard is a great place
for vacations.

294
00:18:41,960 --> 00:18:46,120
Yep, soooo many things to do,
including a very bustling nightlife.

295
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:50,160
I meant about Chickenhare's plans
for his next adventure.

296
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,680
-Oh, it's a good one.
-Really good one.

297
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:55,320
Remember how stunned I was
when we found out?

298
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:57,440
Yeah, you were like...

299
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,760
I didn't look anything like that.

300
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,840
Ohhh yes, you did!
I have a photo perfect memory!

301
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,680
What is he going after?

302
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,400
The Groundhog
With The Backward-Facing- Face.

303
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:11,280
-That's exactly how you looked.
-That's exactly how I looked.

304
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,960
So, will Meg be joining him?

305
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:17,360
I'd assume so. They're so close,
more like siblings than friends really.

306
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:19,920
A simple "yes" would have sufficed.

307
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:25,560
Now that I'm thinking about it.
This is perfect.

308
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:29,520
I will find the Groundhog With
The Backward-Facing-Face first

309
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:33,560
and change the past so that Chickenhare
won't be able to steal Meg from me.

310
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,360
So she and I will be together again.

311
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,040
For eternity!!

312
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,400
Prepare the airship, we're moving out.

313
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:44,000
-Okay boss!
-Okay boss!

314
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,840
Don't be too hard on yourself,
Chickenhare.

315
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,680
I lied to my dad. I stole.

316
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,200
Trust me,
you did it for the right reasons...

317
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,880
For our people, for your people.

318
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,160
You must be kidding!

319
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,320
Why would I?

320
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:15,720
Is that your friends?

321
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,720
They're the best adventurers I know!

322
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:20,600
I'd put my life in their hands
in a heartbeat.

323
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:23,200
Why are you taking this thing on board?

324
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:26,520
Four words: long trip bad sciatica.

325
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:30,400
Meg, Abe, this is Gina, my sister.

326
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:34,720
-Ooh, I see the resemblance.
-I know! Right?!

327
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:39,320
Does nobody in your family get sarcasm
or is that just a recessive gene?

328
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:42,160
Don't pay attention,
he's always like that...

329
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:43,680
Welcome aboard, Gina!

330
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:05,000
Let's give that guy a little room.

331
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:12,840
Abe! You're supposed to be on watch!

332
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:15,040
What-Oh. Sorry,
this armchair is way too comfy...

333
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:19,400
What are you doing? Ooh, come on,
I've become attached to that chair!

334
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,040
Woooow!!!

335
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:32,080
This cartographer,
is he really that good?

336
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:34,880
From what they say, he is the best!

337
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:43,360
See I never wanted to be
a cartographer.

338
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,800
That was all about pleasing my mom.

339
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,440
Always been a people-pleaser.

340
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:49,560
Stop moving!

341
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:50,960
But I just turned eighty, man,

342
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:54,920
and I said, "Carl, it's time
you followed your passion."

343
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,680
Wow, you're remarkably... Consistent.

344
00:22:57,840 --> 00:23:00,360
So, what kind of tattoos
would you guys like?

345
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,200
I can't choose...

346
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:04,040
Don't worry about the price.

347
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:07,280
I'm going to give you guys
the Friends and Family Discount...

348
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:09,920
-Wow. That's...
-So generous.

349
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:15,200
But uh, we were hoping to talk to you
about your old and other... Talent.

350
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:19,960
I gotta say, I would loooove to do
a big snake on your chest.

351
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:22,520
Wow, I'd actually pay full price
for that, Carl.

352
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,640
Uh, can we talk about the map first?

353
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,200
Deal!

354
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,200
Ok, cool!... It belonged to...

355
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:33,480
Queen Ingrid the Indecisive yes,
I recognize her style.

356
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,440
What are you doing?

357
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:40,320
I'm going to look for
phantom settlements.

358
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,920
Intentional errors to signify
the treasures location.

359
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:44,280
She used to do it this way.

360
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:48,280
Ohhh, and whatever's not on that map
is the location of the Groundhog!

361
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:51,520
Waawh. Look who can spell 'cat' when
you spot him the 'C' and the 'A.'

362
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:58,200
See this chain of hills.
They are called the sundial hills.

363
00:23:58,360 --> 00:24:01,600
The nine o'clock hill
has been voluntarily removed.

364
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,960
If you are looking for the treasure,
then it's definitely here.

365
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:08,880
Hmmm strange... An untrained eye would
never have noticed this,

366
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:11,680
but at this exact location,
there is a second error.

367
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:15,720
Something else is buried there. Less
important I would say, but still...

368
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:18,080
Thank you Carl,
you've been a great help!

369
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:21,840
Wowowow, not so fast...
Now let's get down to business.

370
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:23,800
My latest creation...

371
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:26,080
But what the heck is this?

372
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:30,640
There's no way I'm paying for this,
this looks nothing like my love!

373
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:34,200
That looks exactly like Evelyn.
You just don't understand genius.

374
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:38,440
Oh yeah?! Then I'm not the only one
since your other clients just took off.

375
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:39,600
What??

376
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:42,120
Chickenhaaaaare!!!!

377
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:46,200
Phew.. hehe... That was close!

378
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:48,200
Too close.

379
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:51,120
Wait, that building
wasn't there ten minutes ago...

380
00:24:51,280 --> 00:24:52,640
-Hello there!
-Crolloq!

381
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:55,360
-Not her again!
-What are you doing here?

382
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:57,520
I heard you were looking for
the Groundhog...

383
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:02,000
Therefore, so am I...
And for that, I need that map.

384
00:25:05,040 --> 00:25:06,280
Oh by the way...

385
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:08,520
I asked some friends to join the party.

386
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:12,240
Piggies.

387
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,600
That's all we needed...

388
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:18,080
Oooooh, that one is cute!

389
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:24,480
Look, if this is about your god
Santoro, we didn't mean to anger him.

390
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,120
Yeah, yeah. Our bad,

391
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:29,160
we were just trying to not get thrown
into the volcano, eheh.

392
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:32,040
Huuuh, nice try Meg!

393
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,280
Let's go!

394
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,000
This way!

395
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:04,320
-Abe?
-Anyone...? Help?

396
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:05,520
I'm coming!

397
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,040
-Now what?
-Uuuuh, I don't know...

398
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,040
-Whaaw! What a plan!
-Watch out!

399
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:40,640
Ouch! What is this...

400
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:42,480
Hey!! Wakey-Wakey!!

401
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:46,400
What the heck are you doing up there!!

402
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:48,000
Gina, this way!

403
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,320
Uh-oh!

404
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,160
Jump!

405
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:00,840
Ouch!!

406
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,960
-Gina!! You're alright?
-I'm fine.

407
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:19,920
Hey you! We're not done yet!

408
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:36,320
Oh uhh, alright! Come on in hehe!

409
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:49,520
Abe, hurry!!

410
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,200
Is everyone okay?

411
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:02,200
Yeah! We're good.

412
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:06,680
-Chickenhare... We need a plan.
-Alright.

413
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:10,880
Okay, um... If we go to the jungle
first... And then the...

414
00:28:11,040 --> 00:28:12,080
Let's face it, Chickenhare...

415
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:14,960
We won't have time to find
the two treasures before sunset.

416
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:17,080
-We need to split up.
-What?

417
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:19,680
-You and I go for the Groundhog.
-But Meg and Abe...

418
00:28:19,840 --> 00:28:21,920
They'll be fine!
You said it yourself...

419
00:28:22,080 --> 00:28:24,280
They are the best adventurers
you know...

420
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:27,120
You're not pulling right!

421
00:28:27,280 --> 00:28:29,840
-Your shell is too big!
-How dare you?

422
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:33,560
-Okay, it's not that big, it's just...
I don't wanna talk about it...

423
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,600
That's our stop anyway.

424
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:39,440
-We need to split up.
-Sorry, what?!

425
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:41,960
-Must be sunstroke...
-You guys go to the eastern point!

426
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,880
We meet tonight at the beach
to the North.

427
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:46,320
Uuh, uh... Okay...

428
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,360
What? No, it's not...

429
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:53,120
What's the opposite of okay?
Okay not, okay not, okay not!

430
00:28:59,560 --> 00:29:00,920
Chickenhare,

431
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:02,280
we have to go.

432
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:23,360
Remind me to replace Chickenhare
as my Emergency Contact.

433
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:29,680
She'll never let go!

434
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:33,000
Abe, I want you to follow the river,
I'll catch up with you!

435
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:37,040
Hahahah, good one Meg!
Let's abandon Abe once again...

436
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:39,600
Meg??

437
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,120
Let's end this.

438
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,000
Meg?

439
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:03,480
Alright, so... If we go this way,

440
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:07,040
we will be at the nine o'clock hill
before nine o'clock.

441
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:11,160
-Why don't I wrap that better for you.
-It's fine.

442
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:14,760
I don't want to brag, but in Junior
Adventurers, I got the Mummy Award.

443
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:15,960
I said it's fine!

444
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:18,960
Sorry, I was just trying to be...

445
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:20,280
-Nice?
-Brotherly.

446
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:25,360
Thank you. It just hurts, that's all.

447
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:33,040
I think we're getting really close
to finishing each other's sentences.

448
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:35,280
-That's what I was...
-Thinking?

449
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:41,000
This is the way I always hoped
it would be.

450
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,080
What is?

451
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:44,600
When I would find out that
I had a sister or brother.

452
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,240
Tell me more about our family.
What about our father?

453
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:51,920
His name is Grong,
he's our great leader.

454
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:53,320
And... What about our mother?

455
00:30:54,720 --> 00:30:57,840
Her name... Her name was... Elora.

456
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:00,160
Was...?

457
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:02,080
Oh... I see...

458
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:00,920
Where do you think you're going,
little mouse?

459
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:04,440
Well, without your legs,
I guess you won't go very far.

460
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:12,760
Your master trained you well.

461
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:15,720
Oh what am I saying,
I was your master!

462
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:22,280
You want that?

463
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,440
Come get it!

464
00:33:08,080 --> 00:33:09,120
How did you?

465
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:12,720
How? Obviously when you put me
in that hole,

466
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:15,760
the toxic fumes I inhaled daily
made me immune...

467
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,800
To your charms.

468
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:19,880
Ok, you won...

469
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:22,960
-Take it.
-What, you're giving up already?

470
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:32,960
Not so fast!
We're not done yet.

471
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:36,480
How... do you think... fighting me...
is going to make me...

472
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:37,600
want to team up with you again?

473
00:33:37,760 --> 00:33:41,480
It doesn't matter... when I have the
Groundhog... Everything will change.

474
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:44,480
I didn't leave because I wanted another
partner, Crolloq...

475
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,000
I left

476
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:51,760
to get out of your reach.

477
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:08,600
Follow the river.
That's all we gotta do, Abraham.

478
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:11,040
What we don't need to do is focus on
all the sounds

479
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:13,800
in the Never-Ending-Jungle-
that has to be a misnomer, right?

480
00:34:14,040 --> 00:34:16,560
Probably named by someone who was
trying to impress a colleague.

481
00:34:16,720 --> 00:34:19,000
"Oh, you found the Peninsula-That-
Should-Be-An-Island.

482
00:34:19,160 --> 00:34:21,240
Well,
I found the Never-Ending-Jungle--"

483
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,760
What was that?!
Is there somebody there?!

484
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:26,600
Meg, that's you, right?!

485
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:29,760
This is just you messing with me for
some unknown, and sadistic reason?!

486
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:30,840
Right?!

487
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,800
I can't take it!

488
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:36,440
Just come out and finish me off,
pleaaase!

489
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:49,160
Cutie pie again!!

490
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:51,240
Oh, come on don't do that!

491
00:34:53,520 --> 00:34:56,720
How did you find me?
I thought I was rather discreet.

492
00:34:57,840 --> 00:35:00,560
Didn't your friends come with you?
Are you all alone?

493
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:13,200
It's ok...

494
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:17,880
I know what it feels like.
My friends have abandoned me too.

495
00:35:23,520 --> 00:35:25,360
Hey, what if we team up together?

496
00:35:26,720 --> 00:35:30,840
Yeah! A walker like me, a fighter
like you, nothing would stop us.

497
00:35:34,240 --> 00:35:36,000
My name's Abe, what's yours?

498
00:35:37,160 --> 00:35:39,360
"Squeak"... Uh! I love it!

499
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:30,920
In your face!

500
00:36:34,640 --> 00:36:37,240
Are you... Are you a chickenhare too?

501
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:39,520
-Are you a chickenhare?
-We gotta get going--

502
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:41,800
I'm not going anywhere until
you tell me what's going on?

503
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,560
-Chickenhare, we don't have time!
-You lied to me!!!

504
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:45,400
Believe me, I'll explain everything
after we get the Groundhog.

505
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,920
No!! Tell me the truth!

506
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:55,880
I'm not a chickenhare.
I'm a harechicken.

507
00:36:56,680 --> 00:37:01,040
-That's what we call ourselves.
-So everyone on your island...?

508
00:37:01,200 --> 00:37:02,800
They're all harechickens.

509
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:07,480
It all began eons ago,
at that time we were simple hares.

510
00:37:08,320 --> 00:37:10,240
When King Bartolomeo the Impatient

511
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:12,360
summoned our ancestors
to court martial...

512
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:17,000
Our clan will not take part
in your senseless war, King Bartolomeo.

513
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:20,160
You dare to disobey me?!

514
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:25,520
You think you're above me,
but you will pay for your arrogance.

515
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:28,680
I will turn you into monsters...!

516
00:37:38,960 --> 00:37:41,680
They were labeled freaks, monsters.

517
00:37:42,440 --> 00:37:43,920
And so they sailed the seas

518
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:47,240
until they found an island that
was hidden from the known world.

519
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:49,920
And that's where we've lived,
ever since.

520
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:52,760
Why didn't you tell me the truth
from the beginning?

521
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:56,520
I had to make you believe that you were
special, that you were the Chosen One.

522
00:37:56,680 --> 00:37:59,080
No, you didn't.
I would have helped you.

523
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:02,160
Now that I know you better,
I know you would...

524
00:38:03,320 --> 00:38:05,120
If I wasn't the Chosen One,

525
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:08,640
then why did our father choose me
to be adopted by King Peter?

526
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:11,560
Because... You looked more like a hare.

527
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:13,600
Normal.

528
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:26,560
Father thought that King Peter would be
more likely to adopt you...

529
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,240
So while you were living
in Featherbeard as a prince...

530
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:32,040
I was preparing for my role
in our father's plan...

531
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:34,760
To be able to pass as a chicken.

532
00:38:36,760 --> 00:38:40,640
-Gina. You don't have to hide anymore.
-Yes, I have to.

533
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:42,360
You might not remember
how people treated you

534
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,760
before the Hamster of Darkness...

535
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:46,120
Of course, I do!
But things have changed!

536
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:49,600
Good for you! But that's because you're
a prince and a famous adventurer!!

537
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:52,200
-No, that's not true!
-It is!

538
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,400
So spare me the whole

539
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:56,040
"what makes us different
is what makes us special" platitudes.

540
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:59,360
You're not special, Chickenhare,
you're just lucky.

541
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:07,520
Okay. Let's get going.

542
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:39,240
Crolloq, you're okay?

543
00:39:40,640 --> 00:39:42,120
No, ouch...

544
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:51,480
Oh no, nooo.
Noooo!!

545
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,120
-Not again...!!
-Crolloq--

546
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:58,600
There's even less of a sliver
of daylight than last time!

547
00:39:58,760 --> 00:40:00,960
-Crolloq, calm down!
-I can't do it...!

548
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:07,720
... I can't survive another five years
on tiny insects and tiny grubs!

549
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:09,000
Hey hey hey... Look at me...

550
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:11,720
Look at me. Calm down, breathe.

551
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:15,600
That's it... Good!

552
00:40:20,040 --> 00:40:22,720
How'd you lead us into a pit?

553
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:25,000
What?... You were trying to capture me!

554
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:28,600
Well, I wouldn't try if you weren't
running away all the time!

555
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:31,440
Just to make sure... You know
I don't belong to you, right?

556
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:33,680
I care about you!
What's wrong with that?!

557
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:38,480
Seriously, you are not caring Crolloq,
you are possessive and bossy.

558
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:41,480
-Oh, now you're exaggerating-
-I'm not!

559
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:43,360
This is exactly why I had to leave,

560
00:40:43,520 --> 00:40:45,920
because it has never been
a partnership.

561
00:40:46,080 --> 00:40:47,400
It took me some time to
figure that out,

562
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:50,880
but I finally realized that
our relationship was unhealthy.

563
00:40:51,040 --> 00:40:52,320
Unhealthy...?!

564
00:40:52,480 --> 00:40:55,280
Who was protecting you
from Billy Goat Jones at school?

565
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:58,960
And who taught you how to lock the
teachers' restroom from the outside!

566
00:40:59,120 --> 00:41:03,120
Poor Mrs Ableton,
we really were silly teenagers...!

567
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:06,240
I just wanted to keep making memories
like those...

568
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:08,920
To keep pushing the bad ones down.

569
00:41:11,120 --> 00:41:14,320
My mother was right,
I am not good at anything...

570
00:41:15,080 --> 00:41:16,880
Wait, she told you that??!

571
00:41:17,120 --> 00:41:21,600
Just before leaving for the quest of
the Boomerang that Never Returns...

572
00:41:21,760 --> 00:41:23,800
That was the last time I saw her.

573
00:41:24,040 --> 00:41:25,760
She was a great adventurer too,
you know?

574
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,560
You never told me about it...

575
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:30,720
What difference would it have made!
I'm over it now.

576
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:33,560
Plus I brought back more treasures
than she ever found.

577
00:41:34,640 --> 00:41:36,320
The only thing I miss is...

578
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,560
Us.
Together.

579
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:44,200
Crolloq, it's not just about us.
You miss friendships.

580
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:47,760
But you want it so badly
and so desperately

581
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:52,160
that you spoil it by using people
who care for you as mere tools.

582
00:41:52,320 --> 00:41:55,760
So... You've just said that
you cared for me ?

583
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:58,320
I did, and I still do--

584
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:00,440
But in my way, not yours.

585
00:42:00,600 --> 00:42:03,960
I know two little guys who care about
you too, in their own way.

586
00:42:04,120 --> 00:42:07,320
Miggie and Rolf? They're more like
henchmen or gophers.

587
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:10,880
But they are the animals
I am the closest to.

588
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:15,200
And when they're not being totally
annoying or creating havoc everywhere,

589
00:42:15,360 --> 00:42:17,800
they actually are funny...
And warm.

590
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:21,240
I mean, as much as
a cold-blooded animal can be.

591
00:42:22,680 --> 00:42:25,600
But eventually,
I'll probably chase them away too.

592
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:27,520
Well, we're gonna work on that.

593
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,680
No better time to change
than the present.

594
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:31,800
Especially since they are
our only way out!

595
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:34,360
Change?! No, that's not me.

596
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:35,600
Oh! Cool pit...!

597
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,480
I approve! Very dark!

598
00:42:37,720 --> 00:42:38,640
Guyyys!

599
00:42:57,240 --> 00:43:01,600
Don't know where we go
But we take it slow

600
00:43:01,840 --> 00:43:05,040
It is all we know
Just follow in our feet, yeah

601
00:43:05,280 --> 00:43:10,680
Somewhat out of touch
Wanting not so much

602
00:43:11,440 --> 00:43:14,600
Livin', livin', livin' a high life

603
00:43:14,840 --> 00:43:17,320
We're livin' a high life

604
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:21,240
Only you and me
And we're counting up to three

605
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:25,480
We're livin' a high life
We're livin' a high life

606
00:43:26,160 --> 00:43:29,760
Come and see how
We're always out of reach

607
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:33,720
We're livin' a high life
We're livin' a high life

608
00:43:33,880 --> 00:43:40,800
We're livin' a high life
We're livin' a high life

609
00:43:59,600 --> 00:44:00,920
No. Meg told me to wait here!

610
00:44:01,800 --> 00:44:02,800
We're part of a team!

611
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:07,160
No, she does not wipe my butt for me.
I wipe my own, thank you very much.

612
00:44:08,480 --> 00:44:12,040
Oh, really? You're gonna try
reverse psychology on me?

613
00:44:12,200 --> 00:44:14,160
You really think that's gonna work?
Well, it's not!

614
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:23,000
Just so we're clear, I'm not going
because of your reverse psychology!

615
00:44:23,160 --> 00:44:26,200
I'm going because it's not good
for my sciatica to sit for too long.

616
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:32,960
Um, question. Why'd you guys jump
in a pit? That doesn't seem very smart.

617
00:44:33,200 --> 00:44:36,800
Because I missed eating tiny insects
and tinier grubs!

618
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:38,920
Oh, that makes sense.

619
00:44:39,160 --> 00:44:40,800
We fell, you idiots!

620
00:44:43,160 --> 00:44:46,320
Listen, I'm sorry that I just yelled
at you.

621
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:48,640
That I... Always yell at you.

622
00:44:48,800 --> 00:44:51,000
Echo... Echo... Echo... Echo...
Echooooo!

623
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:53,400
I like that. Let me try!
Echo, echo...

624
00:44:53,640 --> 00:44:54,600
Echo...

625
00:44:54,760 --> 00:44:56,640
Would you get a rope?!

626
00:44:56,800 --> 00:44:58,200
I mean, please.

627
00:44:59,160 --> 00:45:02,320
Hold it, I'm having a hard time
understanding you.

628
00:45:02,480 --> 00:45:04,680
It sounded like you said "please".

629
00:45:04,920 --> 00:45:06,200
I did say "please".

630
00:45:06,360 --> 00:45:09,560
Wow boss,
coming from you it feels so unreal...

631
00:45:09,720 --> 00:45:12,840
Yes, believe me, it doesn't feel
natural to me either.

632
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:17,000
But I'm going to need you to please
find us a rope

633
00:45:17,160 --> 00:45:20,440
or at least something long enough
to get us out of here.

634
00:45:21,440 --> 00:45:22,360
Like a stick?

635
00:45:22,640 --> 00:45:24,080
I don't ...

636
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:28,680
A stick, why not...
Anything as long as it is long enough.

637
00:45:28,840 --> 00:45:31,320
Aye-aye, capitaine.
I actually just saw a rope.

638
00:45:31,480 --> 00:45:33,720
Oh, and I saw a stick, I go get it!

639
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:36,680
You're doing good!

640
00:45:37,400 --> 00:45:39,320
That was not a rope,
it was a tree stump

641
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:41,280
but from a distance
it looked like a rope.

642
00:45:41,440 --> 00:45:44,200
-And I found a stick!
-Perfect!

643
00:45:44,360 --> 00:45:45,920
Rolf, give the stick to Miggie.

644
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:49,400
That's right,
now Miggie hits Rolf on the head with--

645
00:45:49,560 --> 00:45:54,440
Whohow, hey! I think what Crolloq means
is that she... She trusts you.

646
00:45:54,680 --> 00:45:55,920
She knows that if you work together,

647
00:45:56,160 --> 00:46:00,440
you will find a way to get us out of
here... If possible before nightfall?

648
00:46:01,240 --> 00:46:02,280
Is that right, boss!

649
00:46:02,520 --> 00:46:06,520
It's true and frankly,
I should've said it a lot more.

650
00:46:06,920 --> 00:46:11,400
As well as I should have told you
how much I valued you guys.

651
00:46:12,520 --> 00:46:16,040
That's the most heartwarming thing
I've ever heard...

652
00:46:16,200 --> 00:46:17,200
Me too!

653
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:22,040
Why... Did you jump?

654
00:46:22,720 --> 00:46:24,280
To save you, boss!

655
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:28,280
Don't worry, Miggie and Rolf
take charge of everything!

656
00:46:38,760 --> 00:46:41,360
I'm going to kill that tattoo artist!

657
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:45,440
Somehow he's even worse with maps
than he is with tattoos...

658
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:49,120
And he was the world's worst
tattoo artist!!

659
00:46:49,280 --> 00:46:51,280
I mean... How could we trust him?

660
00:46:51,440 --> 00:46:54,680
The second we walked into his shop,
I knew we had to be suspicious...

661
00:46:55,320 --> 00:46:58,280
"Stand watch
when the sky's last alight..."

662
00:46:58,440 --> 00:46:59,360
What are you doing?

663
00:46:59,520 --> 00:47:01,840
"... All will be revealed
in plain sight..."

664
00:47:02,000 --> 00:47:03,840
Chickenhare, it's useless...

665
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:08,120
Our sight is the definition of "plain"
and nothing is being revealed.

666
00:47:09,280 --> 00:47:10,360
There it is!

667
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:24,520
-An X always mark the spot.
-What does this mean?

668
00:47:25,480 --> 00:47:26,440
Stand next to me.

669
00:47:35,400 --> 00:47:36,520
Woooowww!

670
00:47:42,600 --> 00:47:46,040
My favorite part of any adventure:
finding the entrance...

671
00:48:00,760 --> 00:48:02,600
-... A shovel?
-It's worse than ours!

672
00:48:02,840 --> 00:48:05,160
Yeah, it's worse than ours.
Maybe you...

673
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:06,360
Dig a hole with it?

674
00:48:18,360 --> 00:48:22,560
Wow guys,
I didn't know you had so much strength!

675
00:48:22,720 --> 00:48:26,080
Looks like these little guys are full
of surprises when given a chance.

676
00:48:26,240 --> 00:48:27,840
Sorry for knocking you out, guys.

677
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:31,400
It's okay. Good luck finding
Chickenhare and Abe!!

678
00:48:33,560 --> 00:48:35,080
What are you going to do now ?

679
00:48:35,240 --> 00:48:39,160
First get my airship back and then...
Well, I don't know yet.

680
00:48:39,400 --> 00:48:41,120
Sounds like a good start.

681
00:48:41,280 --> 00:48:43,880
Thank you Meg,
I'm glad we're friends again.

682
00:48:44,040 --> 00:48:44,960
Me too.

683
00:48:48,760 --> 00:48:52,120
Hey, how long will it take to get
my sense of smell to come back...

684
00:48:52,280 --> 00:48:53,920
Oh me too, me too, can I get one?

685
00:48:54,080 --> 00:48:55,680
Uumm, three to four weeks?!

686
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:58,480
-Let's go guys.
-Ok boss!

687
00:48:58,640 --> 00:49:01,320
-And stop calling me boss!
-Sorry boss!

688
00:49:14,600 --> 00:49:17,880
"Here comes the sun, have a lovely day"

689
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:19,840
The sun?

690
00:49:25,440 --> 00:49:27,400
Don't worry, it's an adventure classic.

691
00:49:27,560 --> 00:49:29,600
Wait... That means we're trapped?

692
00:49:29,840 --> 00:49:32,680
Yep! Now, there is only one way
we can get out:

693
00:49:32,920 --> 00:49:34,280
find the Groundhog!

694
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:47,960
Don't step on the red tiles!

695
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:05,680
I'll never get used to that "classic".

696
00:50:16,040 --> 00:50:19,120
Oh, please don't tell me
we have to go through this!

697
00:50:19,280 --> 00:50:22,080
Not through,
we just have to reach the center.

698
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:24,320
But... It's impossible!

699
00:50:24,480 --> 00:50:28,040
And let me guess... We also have to
carry that "Sun" with us, right?

700
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:31,080
"When the sun rises
on an impossible day,

701
00:50:31,320 --> 00:50:34,880
Keep your eyes closed
and let the tick show you the way."

702
00:50:35,040 --> 00:50:35,960
What?

703
00:50:36,120 --> 00:50:39,000
-This was Queen Ingrid's mantra...
-And so?

704
00:50:39,160 --> 00:50:42,760
And so let us do exactly what she would
have done in a similar situation!

705
00:50:44,240 --> 00:50:45,440
Close your eyes.

706
00:50:48,960 --> 00:50:49,880
Now!

707
00:50:52,840 --> 00:50:54,000
Now!

708
00:51:07,360 --> 00:51:09,880
See! It was nothing impossible!

709
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:22,560
"Choose wisely"

710
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:27,000
-Ingrid was left-handed.
-Yes! It's gotta be the left.

711
00:51:27,160 --> 00:51:30,480
But she wrote with her right hand
after a childhood accident...

712
00:51:30,640 --> 00:51:33,280
-So, it's gotta be the right. Right?!
-Hold on!

713
00:51:33,440 --> 00:51:36,200
Chickenhare, we are running out of time
so make a decision... Quickly!

714
00:51:36,360 --> 00:51:39,960
It's a trick! Ingrid couldn't make up
her mind. So we don't!

715
00:51:40,200 --> 00:51:42,040
What? How can you be so sure about it?

716
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:45,040
That's the whole point of an adventure.

717
00:51:45,280 --> 00:51:46,600
You can never be sure.

718
00:52:05,960 --> 00:52:07,640
Father was right,

719
00:52:07,800 --> 00:52:10,320
only a great adventurer
could have done this.

720
00:52:19,480 --> 00:52:21,720
Go ahead, this is your moment.

721
00:52:33,360 --> 00:52:36,840
The Groundhog with
the Backward-Facing-Face!

722
00:52:43,440 --> 00:52:45,280
Heey come on...

723
00:52:45,520 --> 00:52:47,880
But what's going on here?

724
00:52:48,440 --> 00:52:50,360
Engineer! Engineer!

725
00:52:51,200 --> 00:52:53,800
Hey you! Are you the maintenance guys?

726
00:52:54,960 --> 00:52:56,760
No..

727
00:52:57,080 --> 00:53:00,280
I see nothing's changed in the eons
I've been stuck here -

728
00:53:00,520 --> 00:53:03,520
nobody wants to take
any responsibility!

729
00:53:04,120 --> 00:53:05,160
Gina, get ready to catch it.

730
00:53:05,320 --> 00:53:09,120
Excuse me? Don't you even dare
thinking about it?!

731
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:10,840
Seriously??

732
00:53:11,000 --> 00:53:14,120
I am a magical and powerful
rodeeeent!...

733
00:53:14,280 --> 00:53:15,800
Ouch!

734
00:53:16,520 --> 00:53:17,440
Nice catch...

735
00:53:25,440 --> 00:53:26,360
Watch out!!

736
00:53:28,800 --> 00:53:30,760
Also an "adventure classic", right?

737
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:34,800
Yes, and my least favorite moment...
Reaching the exit.

738
00:53:40,240 --> 00:53:41,360
Stop!!

739
00:53:43,520 --> 00:53:45,840
There used to be a bridge here
3000 years ago...

740
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:47,560
Planned obsolescence, I guess.

741
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,160
On the other hand,
automatic doors work like a charm!

742
00:53:52,320 --> 00:53:53,240
I noticed!

743
00:53:55,920 --> 00:53:58,120
-And now what??
-And now, we fly!!

744
00:53:58,280 --> 00:53:59,480
-What?!
-Seriously??

745
00:53:59,640 --> 00:54:00,920
Well, technically glide.

746
00:54:01,160 --> 00:54:02,680
I can't fly or glide!

747
00:54:04,400 --> 00:54:05,320
No offense.

748
00:54:07,920 --> 00:54:10,360
Open your wings, trust your instinct!

749
00:54:10,520 --> 00:54:11,880
No, I can't!

750
00:54:12,040 --> 00:54:13,560
And that's how everything ends up...

751
00:54:13,800 --> 00:54:16,080
After a 3000 years wait.

752
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:25,000
What was that?

753
00:54:25,240 --> 00:54:29,360
Has the concept of flight changed
in the last thousand years? Ouch!!

754
00:54:29,520 --> 00:54:31,560
Landings are always
the hardest part of flying...

755
00:54:31,720 --> 00:54:33,560
Well, technically the ground is.

756
00:54:33,720 --> 00:54:35,560
Ready, sis?
Let me crack your back.

757
00:54:35,720 --> 00:54:36,640
-No.
-Trust me...

758
00:54:36,800 --> 00:54:37,760
Stop it, Chickenhare!

759
00:54:37,920 --> 00:54:40,720
Stop being nice... Stop being... You.

760
00:54:41,600 --> 00:54:43,960
Uh...Okay... I'll try.

761
00:54:51,320 --> 00:54:54,160
-What are you doing?
-What our father needs me to do.

762
00:54:55,680 --> 00:54:57,840
It's not the tree of life
you want to change...

763
00:54:58,560 --> 00:54:59,760
You want to change us...

764
00:54:59,920 --> 00:55:02,920
It's going to be better
for all of us... To be normal.

765
00:55:03,080 --> 00:55:07,040
Then everything was a lie...
From the beginning.

766
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:10,520
-Are you even my sister?
-I am...

767
00:55:10,760 --> 00:55:13,600
Really? Because you don't actually
behave like one.

768
00:55:13,760 --> 00:55:15,360
-Stop...
-I trusted you!

769
00:55:15,520 --> 00:55:18,560
I left my father, my friends behind
to find that damn Groundhog!

770
00:55:18,720 --> 00:55:19,640
-Hey!!
-Sorry...

771
00:55:19,800 --> 00:55:21,240
Please, stop!

772
00:55:21,400 --> 00:55:25,080
How naive I was...
To have once thought I had a sister.

773
00:55:33,360 --> 00:55:34,880
I'm sorry Chickenhare.

774
00:55:36,520 --> 00:55:37,800
I really am...

775
00:55:52,080 --> 00:55:54,400
Abe? Aaabe?!

776
00:55:57,480 --> 00:55:58,560
Aaabe?

777
00:56:06,160 --> 00:56:07,640
Hey Squeak, pull my finger!

778
00:56:10,280 --> 00:56:12,320
I love an audience that
hasn't been exposed to mass culture!

779
00:56:12,480 --> 00:56:13,800
-Hey guys!
-Gina!

780
00:56:14,480 --> 00:56:15,400
Where is Meg?

781
00:56:15,560 --> 00:56:18,000
She went after the nutty leopard.
Where is Chickenhare?

782
00:56:18,240 --> 00:56:20,920
He's picking up a couple last-minute
provisions. What did you find?

783
00:56:21,160 --> 00:56:24,320
Me and my new buddy here, eheh,
have found the second treasure!!

784
00:56:25,000 --> 00:56:25,960
That's it?

785
00:56:26,120 --> 00:56:30,400
I confirm, THIS is the royal
Earth Mover of Destiny.

786
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:32,480
So THIS the groundhog?

787
00:56:32,720 --> 00:56:35,960
Huh? I demand a bit of respect!
You, little ignorant!

788
00:56:36,120 --> 00:56:37,440
Oh, here comes Chickenhare!

789
00:56:47,680 --> 00:56:49,400
Didn't see that coming.

790
00:56:49,560 --> 00:56:50,720
Squeak!

791
00:56:50,960 --> 00:56:51,880
You...

792
00:57:12,040 --> 00:57:13,720
Chickenhare, are you okay?

793
00:57:13,960 --> 00:57:16,200
Dad, how did you find me?

794
00:57:16,440 --> 00:57:18,640
I did my best.
What happened?

795
00:57:19,840 --> 00:57:21,320
Gina stole the Groundhog.

796
00:57:21,480 --> 00:57:24,800
She's going to use it to change the
curse that made us all harechickens.

797
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:27,440
I'm sorry, Dad.

798
00:57:27,680 --> 00:57:30,160
I thought I was helping them
save their island.

799
00:57:30,960 --> 00:57:33,560
-She lied to me.
-It's okay, son.

800
00:57:33,720 --> 00:57:35,240
I'm so sorry.

801
00:57:35,880 --> 00:57:38,800
I too have my share of responsibility.

802
00:57:38,960 --> 00:57:41,720
I should have taken the time to listen
to you.

803
00:57:44,080 --> 00:57:45,640
What's done is done.

804
00:57:45,880 --> 00:57:49,320
The only thing that matters now
is what we do from now on.

805
00:57:52,760 --> 00:57:53,880
King Peter?

806
00:57:55,840 --> 00:57:57,360
-Meg!
-Chickenhare!!

807
00:57:58,960 --> 00:58:00,760
Am I happy to see you!

808
00:58:00,920 --> 00:58:01,880
Where's Abe?

809
00:58:06,680 --> 00:58:09,320
Abe... Abe... Wake up!

810
00:58:09,480 --> 00:58:12,800
Mommy, I don't want to come inside
for dinner,

811
00:58:13,480 --> 00:58:15,240
I want to play with my friends.

812
00:58:19,880 --> 00:58:20,840
You're late!

813
00:58:22,960 --> 00:58:26,560
-Watch out!!
-Calm you kung-fu down, he's with me!!

814
00:58:26,800 --> 00:58:28,520
-With you?
-Long story.

815
00:58:28,680 --> 00:58:31,200
-The shovel, she took it!
-Who?

816
00:58:35,600 --> 00:58:38,520
As Squeak said, but less politely...
It's that traitor Gina!

817
00:58:39,680 --> 00:58:41,520
-Gina?
-Long story.

818
00:58:41,680 --> 00:58:45,560
This is not good.
We need to stop her at all cost.

819
00:58:45,720 --> 00:58:50,080
This might not be the best time to tell
you that she's way ahead of us and...

820
00:58:50,240 --> 00:58:51,720
Well... She took the last boat!

821
00:58:53,600 --> 00:58:55,880
Yeah, that's why I said
it wouldn't be a great time.

822
00:58:56,040 --> 00:58:57,200
Need a lift?!

823
00:59:03,880 --> 00:59:07,280
-Let me guess... Long story?
-Long story!

824
00:59:53,880 --> 00:59:55,280
It's Gina!

825
00:59:55,440 --> 00:59:56,360
-Gina?
-You sure?

826
00:59:56,520 --> 00:59:58,680
Gina, you're back!

827
00:59:58,920 --> 00:59:59,840
Look at you!

828
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:01,600
We're so glad to see you again!

829
01:00:06,200 --> 01:00:07,280
Father!

830
01:00:08,040 --> 01:00:09,120
Gina!

831
01:00:13,120 --> 01:00:14,240
Do you have it?

832
01:00:14,880 --> 01:00:16,480
Oh... Sure.

833
01:00:22,480 --> 01:00:25,200
-What's that?
-The Magical Earth-Mover of Destiny.

834
01:00:25,360 --> 01:00:26,560
His shovel.

835
01:00:27,880 --> 01:00:28,800
What's it for?

836
01:00:28,960 --> 01:00:31,520
In order for me to change the past,

837
01:00:31,680 --> 01:00:33,880
you must use the Magical Earth-Mover
of Destiny

838
01:00:34,040 --> 01:00:38,120
to dig a womb out of the Earth
that I will emerge from...

839
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:41,560
We have to dig a hole with this shovel?

840
01:00:42,720 --> 01:00:44,800
Yes, you have to dig me a hole.

841
01:00:44,960 --> 01:00:48,480
And after awaking from a night of
restful sleep, I will emerge.

842
01:00:48,640 --> 01:00:52,120
And when I see my shadow
for the first time that day...

843
01:00:52,280 --> 01:00:55,960
Um, well, I suggest
you don't wander off because

844
01:00:56,600 --> 01:00:58,600
magic will happen!

845
01:01:00,400 --> 01:01:01,680
You did it!

846
01:01:01,840 --> 01:01:05,120
Tonight, we feast as harechickens.

847
01:01:05,280 --> 01:01:08,760
Because tomorrow
we become hares again!

848
01:01:17,920 --> 01:01:19,840
Oh, yeaaah! I like it!

849
01:01:20,560 --> 01:01:23,520
Make sure you cover me entirely?
Like that!

850
01:01:23,760 --> 01:01:24,880
That's right!

851
01:01:34,400 --> 01:01:37,720
Three years away has curtailed
your love for root sauce.

852
01:01:38,960 --> 01:01:40,000
I don't blame you.

853
01:01:40,160 --> 01:01:44,560
But thanks to you, our Root Sauce
eating days are coming to an end.

854
01:01:44,720 --> 01:01:46,320
You're a hero, Gina.

855
01:01:46,560 --> 01:01:49,800
-I don't feel like one.
-No, I'm sure you don't.

856
01:01:50,040 --> 01:01:53,520
I imagine you feel awful,
that you betrayed your brother.

857
01:01:53,760 --> 01:01:57,400
But you did it for our people,
for your people.

858
01:01:58,280 --> 01:02:02,160
I can't tell you how many times
over the years I've asked myself,

859
01:02:02,320 --> 01:02:04,760
How could you send your only son away?

860
01:02:05,720 --> 01:02:07,240
And your daughter?

861
01:02:10,120 --> 01:02:12,760
I had to do it. For all of us.

862
01:02:19,240 --> 01:02:21,600
What will you do when you'll face him?

863
01:02:22,160 --> 01:02:26,320
I'll do whatever it takes to get
that scepter away from him.

864
01:02:35,520 --> 01:02:37,120
There! It's her boat!

865
01:02:37,880 --> 01:02:40,920
You're sure it's here?
I don't see any tree on this island...

866
01:02:54,920 --> 01:02:55,840
There!

867
01:02:57,160 --> 01:02:58,520
We'll only have one shot at it.

868
01:02:59,280 --> 01:03:03,640
Oh, Groundhog
with the Backward-Facing-Face,

869
01:03:04,080 --> 01:03:05,440
awaken!

870
01:03:05,600 --> 01:03:10,080
And bask in the rays of
the new day's sun...

871
01:03:15,080 --> 01:03:18,040
Enter my shadooow!

872
01:03:23,320 --> 01:03:24,240
What?

873
01:03:29,360 --> 01:03:31,200
They want the groundhog! Get them!

874
01:03:53,920 --> 01:03:56,560
What? Hey? What's going on?

875
01:03:56,720 --> 01:03:57,720
No!

876
01:04:02,640 --> 01:04:04,240
-Oopsie.
-Doopsie.

877
01:04:27,120 --> 01:04:28,200
Gina!!

878
01:04:59,560 --> 01:05:01,320
Where are we??

879
01:05:03,800 --> 01:05:08,400
Congratulations,
you have opened the corridors of time.

880
01:05:08,560 --> 01:05:11,720
Welcome to your Family Tree!

881
01:05:13,880 --> 01:05:16,240
And now, the present becomes the past!

882
01:05:17,680 --> 01:05:19,000
Time to move on.

883
01:05:21,600 --> 01:05:25,760
Behind those doors are the significant
events of your family's timeline.

884
01:05:26,440 --> 01:05:27,880
I'm your sister, Chickenhare!

885
01:05:37,680 --> 01:05:39,120
Gina, come here!

886
01:05:39,680 --> 01:05:41,160
Give me your hand.

887
01:05:43,040 --> 01:05:44,680
Do you feel him moving?

888
01:05:44,920 --> 01:05:46,680
Oh, mom...

889
01:05:54,800 --> 01:05:56,560
Elora, are you okay?

890
01:05:56,800 --> 01:05:58,440
Yeah, I'm okay.

891
01:05:59,200 --> 01:06:00,200
Mommy!

892
01:06:05,080 --> 01:06:08,840
Promise me that you will do everything
so that our children...

893
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:11,480
Never have to hide from who they are.

894
01:06:11,640 --> 01:06:12,800
I promise.

895
01:06:13,640 --> 01:06:16,280
Elora? Elora nooo!

896
01:06:16,520 --> 01:06:18,120
No...

897
01:06:28,080 --> 01:06:31,400
Ahem. Could we speed up the pace?

898
01:06:33,400 --> 01:06:36,400
-Take me to the rat king.
-We have to go deep.

899
01:06:36,560 --> 01:06:38,120
-Fine.
-Wait!!

900
01:06:58,800 --> 01:07:02,760
I'm your King,
my orders shall not be discussed!

901
01:07:03,000 --> 01:07:06,880
Our clan will not take part in
your senseless war, King Bartolomeo.

902
01:07:07,120 --> 01:07:10,040
But...
We were harechickens before the curse?

903
01:07:11,040 --> 01:07:15,800
You think you're above me,
but you will pay for your arrogance.

904
01:07:16,040 --> 01:07:19,480
I will turn you into monsters!...

905
01:07:20,120 --> 01:07:22,240
By spreading rumors about you.

906
01:07:22,400 --> 01:07:24,920
By blaming every disaster,
every famine, every plague on you.

907
01:07:25,080 --> 01:07:28,160
There is no curse,
we've always been this way.

908
01:07:28,320 --> 01:07:32,080
You'll become unwanted
everywhere you go...

909
01:07:32,680 --> 01:07:33,840
And eventually,

910
01:07:34,000 --> 01:07:37,240
you'll end up hiding yourself
from the world,

911
01:07:37,480 --> 01:07:40,880
all alone in your disgrace.

912
01:07:41,840 --> 01:07:43,600
It was all a lie?!

913
01:07:44,120 --> 01:07:45,240
All this time...

914
01:07:45,400 --> 01:07:48,240
-Gina, are you okay??
-NO, I'm not!

915
01:07:48,480 --> 01:07:49,680
What happens next?

916
01:07:52,760 --> 01:07:55,360
Look, look! Land!

917
01:08:03,600 --> 01:08:05,760
This is our new home!

918
01:08:07,040 --> 01:08:09,960
See, this is how it all began!

919
01:08:10,200 --> 01:08:13,040
The Rat King made us monsters
and since then,

920
01:08:13,280 --> 01:08:16,640
we've stayed hidden from the eyes of
the world for our own safety.

921
01:08:16,880 --> 01:08:19,480
One day, you will replace me

922
01:08:19,640 --> 01:08:23,840
and it will be your duty to protect
our people from the Out There.

923
01:08:36,840 --> 01:08:40,360
This way, we'll be invisible
to those coming from the sea.

924
01:08:43,640 --> 01:08:45,520
What are they doing?

925
01:08:47,960 --> 01:08:49,440
They're bending the tree...

926
01:08:50,320 --> 01:08:52,520
Then, that explains why it got sick!

927
01:08:52,680 --> 01:08:55,560
They do not understand that
I am doing this for their own safety.

928
01:08:55,720 --> 01:08:58,360
They don't know how dangerous
the Rat King is.

929
01:08:58,520 --> 01:09:00,280
He turned us into monsters!

930
01:09:00,520 --> 01:09:04,440
It's my duty to protect my people
from their own naivety.

931
01:09:05,400 --> 01:09:06,880
No!! I can't let that happen!

932
01:09:07,120 --> 01:09:08,920
Gina!! Don't!

933
01:09:14,120 --> 01:09:17,080
We don't have to be ashamed,
we don't need to hide.

934
01:09:18,440 --> 01:09:21,800
He's right,
the problem is not us, it is them!

935
01:09:21,960 --> 01:09:25,160
Yes! Let's stop hiding, let's fight!!

936
01:09:30,360 --> 01:09:31,360
Gina!!

937
01:09:45,320 --> 01:09:47,240
Freedooom!!

938
01:09:48,240 --> 01:09:49,400
No!!

939
01:10:14,320 --> 01:10:15,480
What have I done?

940
01:10:57,160 --> 01:10:59,800
Gina, you're flying!

941
01:11:14,600 --> 01:11:15,800
We're not gonna make it!

942
01:11:17,120 --> 01:11:18,840
-That leaf on the right!
-Copy!

943
01:11:25,480 --> 01:11:26,840
Ahem.

944
01:11:28,120 --> 01:11:29,360
Could we speed up the pace?

945
01:11:32,080 --> 01:11:33,440
-Chickenhare!
-Gina!

946
01:11:34,280 --> 01:11:37,040
I'm sorry...
I'm sorry I lied to you!...

947
01:11:38,040 --> 01:11:40,680
I'm sorry I was so mad at you
for what happened to mom...

948
01:11:40,840 --> 01:11:42,640
I'm sorry for everything I did.

949
01:11:43,320 --> 01:11:45,760
Don't be sorry, I get it now.

950
01:11:47,760 --> 01:11:48,720
What's going on?

951
01:11:51,640 --> 01:11:54,800
It looks like we changed the past
by leaving it like it was.

952
01:11:55,440 --> 01:11:59,200
Well, if you say so. I've never
understood that magic anyway.

953
01:11:59,360 --> 01:12:01,280
I'm just a groundhog after all.

954
01:12:01,440 --> 01:12:03,680
True but, now you're free.

955
01:12:24,360 --> 01:12:27,080
Chickenhare, is that you?

956
01:12:28,240 --> 01:12:29,800
Okay, job is done.

957
01:12:29,960 --> 01:12:33,560
Now if you're looking for me,
you'll find me at the beach.

958
01:12:33,800 --> 01:12:37,000
The Groundhog is free? So that means...

959
01:12:37,240 --> 01:12:38,560
What have you done ?...

960
01:12:38,720 --> 01:12:40,800
Father, I have to talk to you...

961
01:12:41,040 --> 01:12:42,480
To all of you.

962
01:12:43,160 --> 01:12:45,480
The magic took us back 900 years ago.

963
01:12:45,720 --> 01:12:50,680
I saw our clan as I see you now, just
before the Rat King changed our lives.

964
01:12:50,920 --> 01:12:53,120
We were beautiful, proud...

965
01:12:53,360 --> 01:12:56,640
And covered with those flaming feathers
that make us who we are.

966
01:12:58,720 --> 01:13:00,440
You need to believe me!

967
01:13:00,600 --> 01:13:04,520
I have dedicated my entire life to our
cause and I was ready to die for it...

968
01:13:06,280 --> 01:13:11,360
But this cause was a lie perpetrated
by our ancestors, generations ago.

969
01:13:12,520 --> 01:13:14,000
We are not cursed!

970
01:13:14,800 --> 01:13:16,600
We've just
trapped ourselves in a prison.

971
01:13:16,760 --> 01:13:21,000
Not a prison! A shelter!
To protect us from the Out There!

972
01:13:21,160 --> 01:13:22,520
I come from the Out There...

973
01:13:23,160 --> 01:13:25,080
This is the only world
I have ever known

974
01:13:25,320 --> 01:13:27,960
since I was a baby left alone
in a jungle.

975
01:13:28,120 --> 01:13:31,400
And it was someone from the Out There
who took me under his wing.

976
01:13:31,560 --> 01:13:34,960
Who provided me with all the love
a father could give his son.

977
01:13:35,200 --> 01:13:38,920
It was in the Out There that I grew up
with a friend with a heart so big

978
01:13:39,160 --> 01:13:41,400
that even his shell could not hide it.

979
01:13:41,560 --> 01:13:43,600
A friend who always stood by me,

980
01:13:43,760 --> 01:13:47,440
without ever passing the slightest
judgment on my feathers

981
01:13:47,600 --> 01:13:49,120
and chicken feet.

982
01:13:49,280 --> 01:13:50,720
And it was in the Out There

983
01:13:50,960 --> 01:13:54,800
that I met
the strongest and wisest person I know.

984
01:13:54,960 --> 01:13:57,520
She taught me to embrace
who I really was,

985
01:13:57,680 --> 01:14:00,920
to overcome my fears of showing myself
as I am.

986
01:14:01,080 --> 01:14:05,480
I hope that one day, I'll be
as strong and confident as her.

987
01:14:06,840 --> 01:14:09,640
I have a sister and a father.

988
01:14:09,880 --> 01:14:13,000
But it's in the Out There that
I found my family...

989
01:14:14,480 --> 01:14:19,000
It's not a perfect world, and no one
knows what tomorrow will be like,

990
01:14:19,160 --> 01:14:21,800
but I know this. People can change

991
01:14:22,040 --> 01:14:24,440
and become better
when given the chance.

992
01:14:24,680 --> 01:14:28,480
So give the world a chance to see you.

993
01:14:28,640 --> 01:14:29,760
How?

994
01:14:29,920 --> 01:14:34,480
Look at us! We're starving, how could
we ever find the strength to travel?

995
01:14:35,600 --> 01:14:37,960
The first thing we need to do
is free our tree.

996
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:43,840
It is not sick.

997
01:14:54,960 --> 01:14:56,080
Do you mind?

998
01:15:53,560 --> 01:15:54,960
Together!!

999
01:17:12,960 --> 01:17:15,680
This is what every adventure ending
should look like.

1000
01:17:17,640 --> 01:17:20,960
Well, I guess you can have fun with it
one last time, kids...

1001
01:17:21,200 --> 01:17:22,480
Just be careful with it!

1002
01:17:25,000 --> 01:17:27,080
Are you sure you don't want to come
with us?

1003
01:17:27,240 --> 01:17:30,960
I've got some lost time to make up
for... But you'll see me soon.

1004
01:17:31,200 --> 01:17:33,080
I have no doubt about that.

1005
01:17:36,840 --> 01:17:39,160
-We're ready to take off!
-Whenever you are!

1006
01:17:40,040 --> 01:17:42,200
Abe, Squeak, it's time!

1007
01:17:45,040 --> 01:17:47,160
Come anytime, you're family now!

1008
01:17:47,400 --> 01:17:48,520
Thank you, Meg.

1009
01:17:49,280 --> 01:17:51,680
Mm, speaking of family...

1010
01:17:52,920 --> 01:17:56,480
Your mother made this for me.
It's yours now.

1011
01:17:56,640 --> 01:17:58,560
But... She gave it to you...

1012
01:17:59,520 --> 01:18:02,240
She gave me so much more thant this.

1013
01:18:14,280 --> 01:18:17,560
Well...
So I guess it's time for me to...

1014
01:18:17,720 --> 01:18:18,680
-Leave?
-Go?

1015
01:18:20,040 --> 01:18:21,000
I've tried!

1016
01:18:22,040 --> 01:18:23,680
I don't need this to feel close to you.

1017
01:18:24,920 --> 01:18:25,880
I don't either.

1018
01:18:27,040 --> 01:18:28,280
See you soon, brother.

1019
01:19:56,600 --> 01:19:59,320
So... What's the next adventure
on your bucket list, son?

1020
01:19:59,480 --> 01:20:03,040
First, I have a question...
How did you find me on this island ?

1021
01:20:03,200 --> 01:20:06,280
Mmm, well...
Carl gave me the treasure's location..

1022
01:20:06,440 --> 01:20:07,640
Wait, you met Carl ?

1023
01:20:07,800 --> 01:20:11,120
You made him quite angry so... I...

1024
01:20:11,280 --> 01:20:13,240
Kind of sort of had to negotiate.

1025
01:20:13,400 --> 01:20:14,640
He tattoed you.

1026
01:20:14,800 --> 01:20:16,440
What? Noooo!

1027
01:20:17,160 --> 01:20:18,520
Right on the chest!!

1028
01:20:19,480 --> 01:20:20,680
So, what do you think?

1029
01:20:22,400 --> 01:20:23,480
Don't look at it directly!

1030
01:20:23,640 --> 01:20:25,960
And now,
it will stick in my mind forever!